speechtext:
I. In so far as the Canada Employment and Immigration Commission/department records indicate, the reply is:
December 4, 1972-Appointed on a term basis as a CR 6 senior examining officer at the Toronto International Airport;
March 30, 1973-Tenure of employment changed from term to indeterminate status;
April 1, 1976-Position and incumbent reclassified to the PM 1 level;
March 3, 1977-Promoted to the PM 2 level as an immigration counsellor, Canada Immigration Centre, Prescott.
2. Yes. Mr. Gaudet is presently employed as an immigration counsellor at the PM 2 level at the Canada Immigration Centre, Prescott.
His duties are to select and counsel prospective immigrants in Canada and to assess applications by Canadian citizens or residents for sponsorship of relatives; to control and prevent
December 16, 1981

violation of immigration laws; to investigate status of persons in Canada.
